# Vendored dependencies -- the Makefile clones/downloads all of these fresh
# on first build (see the ifeq($(wildcard ...)) blocks near its top), so
# committing them here would just be an untracked-drift-prone copy of
# someone else's upstream repo.
/lvgl
/dr_libs
/tinyalsa
/faad2
/alac
/mbedtls
/cJSON
/dbus
/opus
/lua
/libexecinfo
/jpeg

# theme2 UI assets. This tree mirrors the device layout: everything tracked
# here is copied to /usr/resource/litegui/theme2/ by scripts/repack_upt.sh,
# so a tracked file is exactly a shipped file.
#
# Stock HiBy graphics are proprietary and never redistributed (see README.md's
# own note). Populate those locally from your own device/firmware dump; the
# blanket exclude below keeps them from being committed by accident.
#
# Everything re-included below is this project's own work, each directory
# carrying its own SOURCES.txt recording the upstream icon set and license
# (Phosphor/Lucide MIT, Montserrat OFL) or confirmed absent from a genuine
# stock dump. Excluding everything first, then re-including specific paths one
# directory level at a time -- git won't apply a file-level negation inside a
# directory that is still itself excluded, so each level needs its own `!`
# before the next.
/assets/theme2/*

# Wholly ours, minus the stock files that happen to share the directory.
!/assets/theme2/power_action/
!/assets/theme2/pull_down/
/assets/theme2/pull_down/bg.png
!/assets/theme2/topbar/
/assets/theme2/topbar/*
!/assets/theme2/topbar/lucide_*.png
!/assets/theme2/topbar/LUCIDE_SOURCES.txt
!/assets/theme2/topbar/SOURCES.txt
!/assets/theme2/topbar/aac.png
!/assets/theme2/topbar/sbc.png
!/assets/theme2/topbar/ldac.png
!/assets/theme2/topbar/aptx.png
!/assets/theme2/topbar/aptx_hd.png
!/assets/theme2/topbar/uat.png
# Per-network Wi-Fi signal bars, built as topbar/wifi_connect_<level>.png by
# gui_network.c. Phosphor wifi-*-fill redraws (see SOURCES.txt), byte-different
# from the stock files of the same name.
!/assets/theme2/topbar/wifi_connect_0.png
!/assets/theme2/topbar/wifi_connect_1.png
!/assets/theme2/topbar/wifi_connect_2.png
!/assets/theme2/topbar/wifi_connect_3.png
!/assets/theme2/boot_animation/
/assets/theme2/boot_animation/*
!/assets/theme2/boot_animation/en/
/assets/theme2/boot_animation/en/*
!/assets/theme2/boot_animation/en/0.png
!/assets/theme2/boot_animation/en/0.jpg
!/assets/theme2/boot_animation/en/config.ini
!/assets/theme2/boot_animation/en/push.bat
!/assets/theme2/stream_media/
/assets/theme2/stream_media/*
!/assets/theme2/stream_media/subsonic.png
!/assets/theme2/stream_media/subsonic_s.png
!/assets/theme2/stream_media/download.png
!/assets/theme2/playing_plane/
/assets/theme2/playing_plane/*
!/assets/theme2/playing_plane/airplay_logo_white.png
# Transport buttons drawn for this project, deliberately kept under the stock
# filenames so they drop straight into the existing asset path and both the
# player screen and the quick drawer pick them up with no code change. Both
# are byte-different from the same-named files in a genuine stock dump. The
# rest of this directory is stock artwork and stays excluded.
!/assets/theme2/playing_plane/btn_play.png
!/assets/theme2/playing_plane/btn_pause.png
# Accent-recolored glyph in the player's quality pill (gui_player.c). Drawn
# for this project and absent from a genuine stock dump entirely.
!/assets/theme2/playing_plane/quality_waveform.png
# Wholly ours (SOURCES.txt / LIST_SOURCES.txt), except the tile backgrounds:
# nothing renders those since the wireless tiles went flat, and the main menu
# is the only screen that keeps a per-tile background.
!/assets/theme2/wireless/
/assets/theme2/wireless/bg_*.png
/assets/theme2/wireless/list_bg_*.png

# Wholly ours: this directory does not exist at all in a genuine stock dump
# (diffed directly against one), and carries its own SOURCES.txt + LICENSE
# (Phosphor Icons, MIT). Home/Music/DAC submenu tiles and their gradient
# backgrounds.
!/assets/theme2/submenu/

# Home launcher tiles. Mixed directory: the six tile glyphs and their _s
# duplicates are Phosphor/Material redraws swapped in place (SOURCES.txt),
# each byte-different from the stock file of the same name. The rest of the
# directory (item*.png, hor_line/ver_line, bg_*.png) is either stock or no
# longer rendered, so it stays excluded.
!/assets/theme2/launcher/
/assets/theme2/launcher/*
!/assets/theme2/launcher/SOURCES.txt
!/assets/theme2/launcher/music.png
!/assets/theme2/launcher/music_s.png
!/assets/theme2/launcher/stream_media.png
!/assets/theme2/launcher/stream_media_s.png
!/assets/theme2/launcher/wireless.png
!/assets/theme2/launcher/wireless_s.png
!/assets/theme2/launcher/book.png
!/assets/theme2/launcher/book_s.png
!/assets/theme2/launcher/sys_set.png
!/assets/theme2/launcher/sys_set_s.png
!/assets/theme2/launcher/dac.png
!/assets/theme2/launcher/dac_s.png
# Main menu tile card backgrounds -- the only per-tile backgrounds kept, all
# six absent from a genuine stock dump.
!/assets/theme2/launcher/bg_music.png
!/assets/theme2/launcher/bg_book.png
!/assets/theme2/launcher/bg_dac.png
!/assets/theme2/launcher/bg_stream_media.png
!/assets/theme2/launcher/bg_sys_set.png
!/assets/theme2/launcher/bg_wireless.png

# Settings category rows. Mixed directory: the five icons and their five
# gradient backgrounds are ours (CATEGORY_SOURCES.txt + CATEGORY_LICENSE.txt,
# Phosphor Icons MIT), absent from a genuine stock dump entirely. Everything
# else here (bt, color_*, cursor, gain_*, lo, po, on/off, progress) is stock
# and stays excluded.
!/assets/theme2/settings/
/assets/theme2/settings/*
!/assets/theme2/settings/CATEGORY_SOURCES.txt
!/assets/theme2/settings/CATEGORY_LICENSE.txt
!/assets/theme2/settings/music.png
!/assets/theme2/settings/display.png
!/assets/theme2/settings/power.png
!/assets/theme2/settings/system.png
!/assets/theme2/settings/about.png
!/assets/theme2/settings/bg_music.png
!/assets/theme2/settings/bg_display.png
!/assets/theme2/settings/bg_power.png
!/assets/theme2/settings/bg_system.png
!/assets/theme2/settings/bg_about.png

# Remote-control category icons (src/network/remote_control.c). Mixed
# directory: the four the app resolves are Material Design Icons redraws
# swapped in place (SOURCES.txt), byte-different from stock. item*.png are
# byte-identical to the stock dump and stay excluded, as do the *_s and
# album/explorer/net_radio files nothing resolves.
!/assets/theme2/category/
/assets/theme2/category/*
!/assets/theme2/category/SOURCES.txt
!/assets/theme2/category/all.png
!/assets/theme2/category/artist.png
!/assets/theme2/category/album_artist.png
!/assets/theme2/category/genre.png

# Korean.ttf-derived host-simulator font: excluded, unlike the rest of
# assets/fonts/, because this particular file's own embedded metadata
# doesn't state a license (see assets/fonts/NOTICE.md). Populate locally
# from your own device dump (/usr/resource/fonts/Korean.ttf, subsetted to
# U+1100-11FF,U+3130-318F,U+AC00-D7A3) if you want Korean text to render in
# `make host`'s simulator -- on target this is a non-issue, the real device
# build reads Korean.ttf directly from the stock firmware at runtime.
/assets/fonts/korean.ttf

